<description>&lt;p&gt;Gunmen killed 24 people in attacks in Nigeria and separate assaults left 13 dead on an escorted convoy in Zamfara. Fulani militants hacked 12 Christians to death in Benue and killed additional civilians in Plateau and Niger, while bandits killed an immigration officer and burned his body in Niger. Ansaru terrorists planned an attack on a school in Oyo, and Islamic terrorists assaulted three villages in northeast Nigeria. Russian fighters and the Malian army retook the strategic northern town of Kidal after separatists withdrew. The conflict produced 4,159 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Hindu&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiuAFBVV95cUxQNm52LUpzM3lIbkZoZ19nako3elM0NWgxTE9RSG1lZGQyRURvU2s1alRaX2EwRjFEYkRac2JlNDdHcE1KdFN0aVBoMFMtcnBaZXRRM3kzLU1JWS1EUHU1YmVuVk13b0NZdm5NTkpzRzVGalNLRjBBRzJmLWVaT252MkNJTFpyVnhzTlhnd0Zfb1VhVTZXTGZlakt1VkY2RVdnZVB0VmdrSGV4ZjFhQnVjd2VhbEthY2hx?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Guardian Nigeria News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Le Monde.fr&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxNakE3OGN0MnZyVXc4TzB3azJNSHN4bFlGZi1zLVBZNnhpN1lDQlhRRU9SdEFEMTJrX3R6M2NNTnJ4OWRhM1Z2WkZtNkJjdzlpVHJoWURKMEtpOHJhN2lySzRvY3NCS1dRRTZRcFlFNjU4ODdZbDVTRml1Ymk0a3NzdTNfWE5Nb0VqQWZrelpyRmFfZlVValAzSGswaUk2QzBFOEVNM21sMWhpSmc?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitAFBVV95cUxOREIxRjh4TnhJZzdlVVQxb0JXWUNENlc0UktwVXZzMUF1NkZsZXRCTHp5aU9MdzVoTE9YQlc0M05XUzdNZ3V3ZHZqNjFvX2lsSnlMY1JhczZXSkw1dk16VXdaeEFtSDFQczAyeEVKNGJVa1lIUDg0YW5WRHB4YnlkazlleTRDYjZfc0p2RjJiSWtrcFFHNXlueFVaOFhkMUU0cWpReDh4Q2NzZjA1UWpQbVJhbm4?oc=5&quot;&gt;Punch Newspapers&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/article